Style Fits when For us Batch (a scheduled job writes a file or table) decisions are made on a schedule, scores can be a day old Yes. The account managers work from a monthly list. Real-time API (a service answers one request at a time) a user or system needs an answer within milliseconds No. Nobody is waiting on a screen. <p>Start with the simplest thing that meets the need. If a real-time service were required, the same <code>score_customers</code> function would sit behind a small web endpoint. An illustrative sketch (not run here; it needs a web framework installed):</p> <pre># Illustrative only. Requires: pip install fastapi uvicorn
from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException
import pandas as pd
from mlp_data import serving

app = FastAPI()
model, card = serving.load_model("models/", "repurchase_logistic_v1")      # verified once, at start-up

@app.post("/score")
def score(transactions: list[dict], cutoff: str):
    try:
        return serving.score_customers(model, pd.DataFrame(transactions), pd.DataFrame(), cutoff).head(200).to_dict("records")
    except ValueError as e:                    # bad input -&gt; a clear 422, never a stack trace
        raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=str(e))
</pre>
